Date: 2026-04-01 (update 7 — Registration → Onboarding wizard redirect fix)

## Bug Fixed: New Registration Bypassing Onboarding Wizard

### Root Cause

After registration, `authService.register()` returns the new user (with `tenantId: null`).
`setUser(result.user)` is called immediately — this triggers the `useEffect` guard in
`register/page.tsx` which blindly did `router.replace("/dashboard")`, racing with and
overriding the explicit `router.push("/onboarding")` that followed.

### Files Changed

- `frontend-tenant/src/app/register/page.tsx`
  - `useEffect` guard updated: `user.tenantId === null` → `/onboarding`; else → `/dashboard`
- `frontend-tenant/src/app/onboarding/page.tsx`
  - New auth guard: unauthenticated → `/register`; `user.tenantId` already set → `/dashboard`
  - `handleNext` on `WizardStep.REVIEW`: after `completeWizard()`, calls `authService.me()`
    to refresh `user` in auth store with the newly assigned `tenantId` — prevents redirect
    loop back to onboarding on next navigation

### Flow (correct)

```
/register → register() → user{tenantId:null} → /onboarding
/onboarding → wizard steps → completeWizard() → me() → user{tenantId:"..."} → /dashboard
```

### Status: ✅ Complete. TypeScript 0 errors.

